{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $f(x)$ includes $\\sin(x)$.\n\nRemember that the derivative of $\\sin(x)$ is $\\cos(x)$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\sin(x)]=\\cos(x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[2x-3\\sin(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x)-3\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\sin(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2\\cdot1-3\\cdot\\cos(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2-3\\cos(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$f'(x)=2-3\\cos(x)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=2x-3\\sin(x)$.\n\n$f'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"2-3\\cos\\left(x\\right)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
